  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_ac26c6204b014e3aaa33865a6312c4cc",
      "statement": "The monorepo is organized around an OS analogy: packages/workshop-backend is the kernel that connects users to gadgets and gatekeepers while enforcing sandboxing and access control, packages/gatekeeper-* are the device drivers, and packages/workshop-frontend is the shell.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L97-L108",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b20149b8e3b72f6b03a93c32e922871ea12d9800b1a3286474dacb1a0c046daa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_42f27fadfb2c4272af329db55dbba052",
      "statement": "Every workspace is its own Durable Object, every Gadget runs in a Dynamic Worker Facet, and Gatekeepers install facets into each workspace to manage access to remote services; the stack can also run entirely on the open-source workerd runtime (which is what pnpm run-local does under wrangler).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L116-L116",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d661977734f3f340f9f72aa5f02f49b470d20acda8e45db34d1beb99f754e07c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c16d12801e4e4891baef1f90312a15a4",
      "statement": "The router Worker is a deployment's public origin and its routing config is its binding set: gatekeepers are discovered by scanning GATEKEEPER_* service bindings and mounted at /gatekeeper/<name>/*, while /api* and /blueprint-screenshot/* go to WORKSHOP_BACKEND and remaining paths go to frontend assets (falling through to the backend in dev).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/router/src/index.ts#L1-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c7c0f2979487f98a9badcb46718aaca6730929bbefea59c4aea330892c3245fa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f3b7b05a45a245bbabc2da35791b7ff3",
      "statement": "The backend Worker's Durable Object classes are UserDurableObject, OverseerDurableObject, AdminSettings, and PendingLogin, declared via wrangler migrations and reached dynamically through ctx.exports rather than an explicit durable_objects binding.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/wrangler.jsonc#L47-L63",
